{
  "id": "chaining-adjectives",
  "title": "Chaining Adjectives : くて / で",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "To describe something with two or more qualities, connect adjectives using their **て-form**. The rule differs by adjective type: い-adjectives use くて, な-adjectives use で."
    },
    {
      "type": "pattern",
      "lines": [
        "い-adjective: [stem] + **くて** + [next clause]",
        "な-adjective: [な-adj] + **で** + [next clause]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_table",
      "columns": [
        "japanese",
        "english"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "japanese": "安い → 安くて",
          "english": "cheap → cheap and…"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "面白い → 面白くて",
          "english": "interesting → interesting and…"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "静か → 静かで",
          "english": "quiet → quiet and…"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "便利 → 便利で",
          "english": "convenient → convenient and…"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "example_table",
      "columns": [
        "japanese",
        "romaji",
        "english"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "japanese": "安くておいしいです。",
          "romaji": "Yasukute oishii desu.",
          "english": "It's cheap and delicious."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "静かで広い部屋です。",
          "romaji": "Shizuka de hiroi heya desu.",
          "english": "It's a quiet and spacious room."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "この映画は長くてつまらなかったです。",
          "romaji": "Kono eiga wa nagakute tsumaranakatta desu.",
          "english": "This movie was long and boring."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "彼女は親切で頭がいいです。",
          "romaji": "Kanojo wa shinsetsu de atama ga ii desu.",
          "english": "She is kind and smart."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "content": "The chained form expresses a neutral list : \"X and Y\" : not a causal connection. To say \"it's cheap *so* I'll buy it,\" use から or ので, not くて."
    }
  ]
}